WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.810
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.070
That looks so good...

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.490
Are you ready to order?

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.320
Yeah, uhh, I'll take the grilled fish set!

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.160
I'm terribly sorry, we've run out of fish for today.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.120
What?!

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.870
<i>When I was back home in Okayama,
we ate fish so much I was sick of it.</i>

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:29.000
<i>Ever since I moved out to Tokyo, though,
I've hardly had any and now it's all I want...</i>

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.510
<i>What I would give for that...</i>

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.010
<i>I think I might be homesick!</i>

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.760
Tonight I'm having fish and that's that!

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.440
Sold out?!

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.110
We're having fish tonight!

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.080
Aww, I wanted meat!

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.490
Ahh! My fish!

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.500
I'm home...

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.250
Here we are, fresh grilled atka mackerel!

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.480
Yipee!

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.970
Oh, welcome home, Michiru-chan.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.600
Nao-san! You could at least stop eating for a second!

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.520
What's with this whole box-load of fish?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.770
It all came in a package for Nao-chan from her parents.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.150
You're from Hokkaido?!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.400
Stop eating for a second and use real words!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.900
Fine whatever! Can I just have some of that?!

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.240
Kae-san not you too...!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.040
<i>Focus Michiru...</i>

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.290
<i>Pull back the bones...</i>

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.790
<i>And all that's left is the pure white goodness below...</i>

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.670
<i>Break off one big bite...!</i>

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.170
<i>This is so indulgent...</i>

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.970
<i>Almost spoiling myself but...!</i>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.470
<i>There's no turning back now!</i>

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.060
<i>Freed from my misery at last!</i>

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.270
<i>Oh, how I have longed for the taste of fish all day.
Finally I have found solace!</i>

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.690
I'll be cooking up plenty today,
so don't hold back now okay?

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.320
Thank you so much!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.360
I never realized you two were from the far north, though.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.820
Huh? We never told you?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:47.450
I came out this way right when Makoto
moved here for school.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.460
Fate has kept us together indeed, hasn't it, Makoto?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.250
I would have preferred to live alone to be honest.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.260
You would just cry and beg me to stay with you,
so it's not like I had much choice.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.050
You didn't want to?!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:05.220
Everyone knew us back home
as a couple of adorable close-knit sisters!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.560
We'd get offers from modeling agencies.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.720
Oh my, little ol' me?

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.810
We were actually talking to your sister there...

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:12.730
Wha...?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.770
Sometimes from TV staff.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.770
Oh no, I could never do that!

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.400
We actually wanted to talk to your sister there...

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.150
Wha...?

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.030
They all came for you!
What was I, just an added bonus?!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.910
Took you long enough to realize it.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.200
So cruel!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.160
And look Michiru is just wolfing down that fish
and not listening to a word I say!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.420
Oh! Sorry, it's just so good...

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.050
Michiru-chan, are you more
of a meat-eater or a fish-eater?

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.470
If you had asked me just a while back,
I would have said meat for sure.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.390
But lately, I've really taken a liking to fish too.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.050
Oh-ho-ho...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.430
Well, then, I guess that means you're one of us then.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:56.100
I am captain of the "Fish and Sake Pairing Crew"!

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.060
And you are all my crewmates!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.570
Well that's news to me, you know.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.570
You're the only member.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.570
So be it then! I'll drink alone!

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.660
Is that sake any good?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.080
It is indeed, my soon-to-be-crewmate!

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.580
Just one bite of this...

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.090
And just before that delicious aftertaste
of the fish fades away...

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.710
Captain!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:28.140
The splendid fragrance dances on the nose
before you even take the first sip!

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:33.270
And when that sip is taken, the pure sweetness
of it all washes right over the tongue!

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:37.020
And those delicious little fishies
swim right through that sea of sake!

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.690
Doesn't that fishy taste conflict with the alcohol?

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.060
Not at all!

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:43.440
Really now...?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.110
So what do you say? Ready for a go?
Of course you are!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.360
Huh? Oh uh...

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.370
Please just say yes for me!

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.620
I don't wanna drink all alone!

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.950
Okay, okay! Just stop crying please!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.160
Welcome to the crew!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.180
<i>One of us sure is thrilled about this...</i>

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.250
It does smell really good, though.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.510
Like a pear, or some other kind of fruit...

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:08.430
Who would have thought fermented rice
would smell so sweet?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.140
It's so... pleasant!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:23.650
That refined, fatty fish taste
really helps bring out the flavor!

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.990
Exactly!

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.410
Good to have you with us, Vice-captain!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.160
<i>Talk about the fast-track!</i>

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:36.290
I haven't had much sake before,
but even I can tell this is great.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.170
Dassai!

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:50.890
This is a brand that has won over
sake lovers and haters alike!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:55.060
There's no question about it,
it's the sort of sake anyone can enjoy!

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.970
Dassai?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.520
That's such a strange name, huh?

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.190
The first character means otter.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.860
The second means festival.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.690
Dassai literally means "otter festival"!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:10.660
Apparently the way otters line up their catch,
makes it look like they're having a little festival!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:16.290
It's also a word used to describe how poets line up
reference material when composing.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.330
Like a festival...?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.830
Now then, what shall I whip up next?

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.540
Kind of like that, then, huh?

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.090
Pretty much, yeah.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.590
What does that 50 there stand for?

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.800
Well now! Have I piqued your interest too, Matoko?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.220
That number there shows what percentage
of the rice used was polished.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.310
The more the rice gets polished,

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.940
the more it is worn down and gets smaller,
leaving only the white center.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.900
That makes it much more fragrant!

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.110
There are lots of different types of Dassai
with different polished rice levels.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:51.200
The lower the number, the higher the price!

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.950
Migaki Niwari Sanbu is polished down to 23%!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:00.040
It must be so tiny when polished down that much...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.320
When you get down to "Migaki Sono Saki E",

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:06.250
they don't even make public how much it is polished.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:10.510
<i>It's a top tier sort of sake! If I ever bought any,
I would keep every last drop to myself!</i>

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.260
<i>What's she thinking about
with such a twisted look on her face...?</i>

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:17.510
I bet such a high-grade sake would be just divine.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.930
W-well of course I'd share it, you know!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.230
I'll save up and buy some!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.760
Think of it as my way of saying thanks for all this fish!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:30.440
Yeah... let's all share some...

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.780
<i>She has a heart of gold...</i>

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.820
I've just finished up our next dish!

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:36.910
It's boiled cod.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.910
Mmm! So soft and juicy!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:46.170
And if you follow it up with a little Dassai...

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.170
<i>It's made of rice, of course it makes for the perfect match!</i>

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:52.300
<i>You can almost smell the lush rice itself...</i>

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:55.930
<i>It blends so well, leaving nothing
but the most refreshing taste behind!</i>

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:00.560
The captain of the Fish and Sake Pairing Crew
has met her match...

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.270
Vice-captain what's your situation?

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:07.730
I never would have imagined a bite of fish
and a sip of sake could bring one such bliss.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.570
I can hardly contain myself...!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.150
<i>That was almost erotic...</i>

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.700
Today's gathering of the Fish and Sake Pairing Crew
is now at an end!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:22.290
I'm gonna go give my mom a call.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.500
Be sure to thank her for all of this!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.080
Yup!

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.790
Hi, Mom. Thanks for all the fish! It was good!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:33.510
Hey Mom? Can you send some dessert next time too?

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.050
Are you seriously still hungry?!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.800
What should I do for lunch today...?

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.720
Oh, Amatsuki-san.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.970
Care to join me for lunch?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.730
<i>It's Hanamori-san from the team next to mine!</i>

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.230
Oh, absolutely!

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.190
I think I'll get the grilled fish set.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.530
Oh, are you big on seafood?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.860
Quite the "refined" choice.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:57.990
It's not what you think!
It's really good, you should try it!

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.700
You know it's not so bad every now and then!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.250
I'm so glad you liked it!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.250
With a lunch like this, I'm spoiling myself!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.000
<i>Now then, bring on the rest of the workday!</i>

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.170
What's the matter, Amatsuki-san?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.720
<i>I could go for some sake right about now...</i>

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.270
And so it was, that Michiru expanded
her drinking horizons.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.150
Dassai is made from
a type of rice called "Yamada Nishiki."

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.570
As it all gets polished up to be extra delicious,

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:06.740
it leaves behind about 5,000 tons of rice bran each year.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:12.710
To make use of all that apparently they make things
like rice milk, rice crackers and stuff like that!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.580
Here's to another night!
